            "createdOn": 1754558277,
            "author": {
                "name": "Yang Chen",
                "email": "yang.chen@quantatw.com",
                "username": "Quanta-YangChen"
            },
            "kind": "REWORK",
            "comments": [
                {
                    "file": "configurations/meta/minerva_cmm_misc_boards.json",
                    "line": 23,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Jagpal S Gill",
                        "email": "paligill@gmail.com",
                        "username": "jagpalgill"
                    },
                    "message": "Did someone request for this change?"
                },
                {
                    "file": "configurations/meta/minerva_cmm_misc_boards.json",
                    "line": 23,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Yang Chen",
                        "email": "yang.chen@quantatw.com",
                        "username": "Quanta-YangChen"
                    },
                    "message": "Our SIT team has identified an issue concerning the Redfish path at https://localhost/redfish/v1/Chassis/, where those cables (BCBCableBottom, BCBCableTop, CableCartridgeBottom, CableCartridgeTop) are currently shown. Would it be preferable for cable-related data to be exposed under https://localhost/redfish/v1/Cables/ instead? Please let us know your thoughts."
                },
                {
                    "file": "configurations/meta/minerva_cmm_misc_boards.json",
                    "line": 23,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Jagpal S Gill",
                        "email": "paligill@gmail.com",
                        "username": "jagpalgill"
                    },
                    "message": "@vvlprabha@gmail.com Please look into this (discuss with X functionals) and see what should this get mapped to as per the Inventory type solution you are working on. Should these be Cables or just boards."
                },
                {
                    "file": "configurations/meta/minerva_cmm_misc_boards.json",
                    "line": 23,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Patrick Williams",
                        "email": "patrick@stwcx.xyz",
                        "username": "williamspatrick"
                    },
                    "message": "I've been told elsewhere that a \"CableCard\" is a PCB and not a cable.  If it is a PCB, \"Chassis\" is the correct spot for it.  Boards in Redfish are considered a type of \"Chassiss\"."
                },
                {
                    "file": "configurations/meta/minerva_cmm_misc_boards.json",
                    "line": 23,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Prabha Veerubhotla",
                        "email": "vvlprabha@gmail.com",
                        "username": "Prabha-Veerubhotla"
                    },
                    "message": "@paligill@gmail.com since BCBCable* are actual cables, we can change them to `Cable`. \nCableCartridge* is actually a cartridge if it has PCB we can do `Board`, otherwise we can do `Cable`."
                },
                {
                    "file": "configurations/meta/minerva_cmm_misc_boards.json",
                    "line": 23,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Jagpal S Gill",
                        "email": "paligill@gmail.com",
                        "username": "jagpalgill"
                    },
                    "message": "@vvlprabha@gmail.com BCBCable we can model as Cable and lets model CableCartridge as chassis as Patrick mentioned in Redfish it will eventually become a chassis (for Board)."
                },
                {
                    "file": "configurations/meta/minerva_cmm_misc_boards.json",
                    "line": 23,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Prabha Veerubhotla",
                        "email": "vvlprabha@gmail.com",
                        "username": "Prabha-Veerubhotla"
                    },
                    "message": "@yang.chen@quantatw.com please update the gerrit accordingly."
                },
                {
                    "file": "configurations/meta/minerva_cmm_misc_boards.json",
                    "line": 23,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Yang Chen",
                        "email": "yang.chen@quantatw.com",
                        "username": "Quanta-YangChen"
                    },
                    "message": "Done"
                },
                {
                    "file": "configurations/meta/minerva_cmm_misc_boards.json",
                    "line": 23,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Prabha Veerubhotla",
                        "email": "vvlprabha@gmail.com",
                        "username": "Prabha-Veerubhotla"
                    },
                    "message": "@yang.chen@quantatw.com\n\nBCBCable* type looks fine. @paligill@gmail.com asked to update CableCartridge* type to Chassis. \n\nplease update that."
                },
                {
                    "file": "configurations/meta/minerva_cmm_misc_boards.json",
                    "line": 23,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Yang Chen",
                        "email": "yang.chen@quantatw.com",
                        "username": "Quanta-YangChen"
                    },
                    "message": "Hi @vvlprabha@gmail.com,\nThanks for the reminder. I understood Patrick to mean that \"CableCard\" refers to a PCB and should be considered a chassis, and that boards in Redfish are treated as a type of chassis. Therefore, I kept the CableCard setting as \"Board.\" If I misunderstood, please let me know."
                }
            ],
